American Chemical Society

heavy-metal pollutants linked to particulate matter, especially
in catchments with high levels of pollution, is flooding.
Particularly in the early stages of floods, the concentrations of
suspended particle matter and pollutant contents rise in such
river systems as discharge increases.6,7 Because an increase in
the water content of polluted soils causes changes in their
physicochemical properties, flooding events in floodplains are
particularly concerning.8 The potential accumulation of heavy
metals such as Cd, Pb, Cu, Ni, Mn, and Zn into agricultural
