14:Kidney vetch (Anthyllis vulneraria L.) is a well-known Zn hyperaccumulator. Zn often occurs with Pb in one ore; thus, plants
15:inhabiting waste dumps are exposed not only to Zn but also to Pb toxicity. While the response of kidney vetch to Zn toxicity is
16:relatively well known, the Pb survival strategy of Anthyllis vulneraria has not been the subject of investigations. The aim of
